WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.060
Plants on a mountain slope often look different from lowland relatives.

2
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.160
Are those differences written in their genes, or shaped by where they grow?

3
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.080
Watching them in place cannot tell.

4
00:00:15.083 --> 00:00:20.643
To separate them, raise both populations in one shared environment, a common garden.

5
00:00:22.003 --> 00:00:25.483
Any difference that persists there supports an inherited basis.

6
00:00:26.823 --> 00:00:30.143
If they grow alike, the difference likely came from surroundings.

7
00:00:31.903 --> 00:00:37.143
Inherited variation within one population does not show that two populations differ

8
00:00:37.143 --> 00:00:38.143
genetically.

9
00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:44.227
Next, move organisms both ways between home sites in a reciprocal transplant,

10
00:00:44.787 --> 00:00:46.147
keeping controls at home.

11
00:00:47.507 --> 00:00:49.947
Then you measure how each group fares in both places.

12
00:00:51.307 --> 00:00:55.967
The core idea: – match or swap environments to separate genes from surroundings.

13
00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:01.910
With animals, swap parents instead of soil, a method called cross-fostering.

14
00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.150
Soon after laying, swap eggs between deep-beaked and shallow-beaked pairs, leaving

15
00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.430
other clutches at home.

16
00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.030
Measure chicks as adults.

17
00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:18.290
Predict: if genes alone drive beak depth, how should chicks match genetic and foster

18
00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:19.290
parents? How should chicks match genetic and foster parents?

19
00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:29.653
If genes alone matter, the genetic-parent slope is positive while the foster-parent

20
00:01:29.653 --> 00:01:30.813
slope sits near zero.

21
00:01:32.173 --> 00:01:34.673
If rearing alone matters, those slopes reverse.

22
00:01:36.073 --> 00:01:38.553
If both contribute, both slopes are positive.

23
00:01:39.953 --> 00:01:43.633
Comparing them, with uncertainty, shows roughly how much each matters.

24
00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:48.207
Swaps still have limits, because early environments linger.

25
00:01:49.607 --> 00:01:53.887
Bird eggs are swapped after laying, so effects of the mother through the egg remain.

26
00:01:55.587 --> 00:01:57.767
Foster nests still differ in territory and food.

27
00:01:59.087 --> 00:02:04.987
In mice, cross-fostering pups controls nursing, not prenatal exposure; controlling

28
00:02:04.987 --> 00:02:07.347
the uterus requires transferring embryos.

29
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:13.450
Guard against bias: start groups under matching conditions and assign them at

30
00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:19.490
random. A finch swap on one island belongs to that island and year; different seeds

31
00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:26.030
can shift it. And elevation changes many conditions at once, so temperature cannot

32
00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:27.470
be separated from the rest.

33
00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:32.810
Even with those limits, transplants tested what sets species' ranges.

34
00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:39.570
A niche is where long-run λ, the yearly births-and-deaths growth factor, stays at

35
00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:40.890
least 1 without immigrants.

36
00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:48.150
Amy Angert and Douglas Schemske grew two California monkeyflowers: low-elevation

37
00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:51.610
Mimulus cardinalis and high-elevation Mimulus lewisii.

38
00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:58.470
In gardens inside and beyond each range, both had zero or near-zero fitness past

39
00:02:58.470 --> 00:02:59.470
their limits.

40
00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:01.633
That fits niche limits.

41
00:03:02.973 --> 00:03:09.833
In 2014, Anna Hargreaves, Karen Samis and Christopher Eckert pooled 111 beyond-range

42
00:03:09.833 --> 00:03:15.153
transplant tests. In three quarters, performance fell beyond the edge.

43
00:03:16.413 --> 00:03:19.993
In 46%, the range limit sat at a niche limit.

44
00:03:21.017 --> 00:03:27.557
26%, mostly latitudinal or longitudinal, sustained themselves beyond the range,

45
00:03:27.557 --> 00:03:31.897
fitting dispersal limitation: suitable places never reached.

46
00:03:33.157 --> 00:03:39.877
23%, all at elevation limits, were sinks: immigrants sustain them despite λ below 1.

47
00:03:40.997 --> 00:03:42.917
The shares do not add to 100%.

48
00:03:42.917 --> 00:03:48.357
percent. Control or swap environments, and genes separate from surroundings.
